@page "/download"
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

@* Public by necessity: this is the page a worker opens on their own phone, before they have
   an account and usually before they have heard of Zazi. Anything behind sign-in here would be
   unreachable by exactly the person it is for. Kept to one screen and one button — it is read
   standing at a counter on a borrowed handset. *@

<PageTitle>Get the Zazi app · Zazi</PageTitle>

<div class="legal">
    <h1>Get the Zazi app</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        For the phone that records transactions. Android 8 or newer. Zazi is not on the Play
        Store yet, so it installs from here.
    </p>

    <p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/download/zazi.apk" download>Download Zazi @Version</a>
    </p>
    <p class="muted">About 22&nbsp;MB. On a slow connection give it a minute.</p>

    <h2>Installing it</h2>
    <ol>
        <li>Tap <strong>Download</strong> above, then open the file when it finishes.</li>
        <li>
            Android will say it cannot install apps from this source. Tap
            <strong>Settings</strong> on that message, turn on <strong>Allow from this
            source</strong>, then press back and tap <strong>Install</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>Open Zazi.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="muted">
        That warning is normal for any app not yet on the Play Store. It is asking whether you
        trust where the file came from, not telling you something is wrong with it.
    </p>

    <h2>Signing in</h2>
    <p>
        If you own the business, sign in with the email address and password you signed up with.
    </p>
    <p>
        If you work for one, you do not need an email address or a password. Ask the owner for
        an <strong>activation code</strong> from their Team page, tap
        <strong>I have an activation code</strong>, and type it in.
    </p>

    <h2>What it does on the phone</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Records each transaction as the network's own message arrives, so nothing is missed at a busy counter.</li>
        <li>Keeps working with no signal, and sends everything once there is data again.</li>
        <li>At the end of the day you count your cash and float, and Zazi says whether it agrees.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">
        Zazi records mobile money. It does not move it. You keep using MTN, Telecel and
        AirtelTigo exactly as you do now. <a href="/privacy">What Zazi holds</a>.
    </p>
</div>

@code {
    // Stated so somebody can tell what they are about to install, and so support can tell what
    // somebody already has. Matches versionName in the Android build.
    private const string Version = "2.8.2";
}
